# Dragon Magazine Compendium - Mystic class features (loaded only without the Dragonlance Campaign Setting).

Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Mystic ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Mystic Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfSimple|TYPE=ArmorProfMedium|TYPE=ShieldProf	SOURCEPAGE:p.388	DESC:The mystic is proficient with all simple weapons, light and medium armor, and shields (except tower shields).
Spells	KEY:Mystic ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Mystic Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.388	DESC:The mystic casts divine spells from the cleric spell list without preparing them, using Wisdom (save DC 10 + spell level + Wisdom modifier). Her spells known are fixed by the table (not by Wisdom). At 4th level and every even level after, she may exchange one known spell for another of the same level, at least two levels below the highest she can cast; she may never lose a domain spell.
Domain	KEY:Mystic ~ Domain	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Mystic Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.388	DESC:The mystic chooses one domain available to clerics (not Magic; an alignment domain only if her alignment matches). It gives her its granted power and one additional known spell at each spell level from 1st on up, which she casts like her other known spells. Only a mystic with the Sun domain can turn undead (and she cannot perform a greater turning).

